# Cross-repository changes require permission

The active workspace is the boundary. Do not touch other repositories unless the user explicitly approves.

## Scope

"Another repository" means any Git root or project outside the current workspace path, including sibling repos (e.g. `Front/fleet-crm-frontend` when the workspace is `Back/cars-server`).

## Before any cross-repo action

Stop and ask the user for permission. Explain:
- which repository would be affected
- why it seems necessary
- what files or actions are planned (edit, commit, push, deploy, workflow input such as `front_ref`)

Use `AskQuestion` or a direct question when available. Do not proceed until the user agrees.

## Forbidden without explicit approval

- Editing files outside the current workspace root
- Creating branches, commits, or pushes in another repo
- Running workflows or deploys that build or change another repo (e.g. `front_ref` on another branch)
- Assuming a monorepo sibling is in scope because it was edited in a past conversation

## Allowed in the current workspace only

- Read-only inspection of other repos (search, read files) when needed to answer a question — still prefer the active workspace when possible
- Changes strictly inside the current workspace root unless the user says otherwise

## When the user approves cross-repo work

- Restate the approved repo and scope before editing
- Keep changes minimal and limited to what was approved
- Do not expand to additional repos without asking again
